 :deps {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version "1.12.0"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir.git"
         :git/sha "d809f284c40cc6b4b4de037baf5f9c7a9607e9c3"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-gmir
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotoba-gmir.git"
         :git/sha "323bfc0539036fc101c978121c27f969e257c492"}
        ;; kotoba-mir 4bf67c0: call+loop uses the scanner (:call-live), the
        ;; conservative fallback colors frame slots from CFG liveness, and
        ;; pure integer SSA segments are scheduled per basic block after physical
        ;; allocation behind hard effect barriers, with RAW/WAR/WAW physical
        ;; register hazards preserved. NBB guards integer immediates before
        ;; physical-register hash lookup. Released callee-saved registers stay in
        ;; the preserved tier and are reused before adding another frame save.
        ;; On AArch64, entry parameters live across a call start in that
        ;; preserved tier, avoiding a store/reload pair on every loop iteration.
        ;; Unique-use zero equality followed by branch-zero becomes an explicit
        ;; AArch64-only branch-nonzero while SSA identities are still available.
        ;; AArch64 self-tail edges now receive the allocator's explicit
        ;; parameter-home vector and use its cycle-safe parallel-copy schedule;
        ;; backed/incomplete sites retain the public-entry tail path. x86 retains
        ;; its execution-qualified scratch-first selection. A unique-use integer
        ;; producer in one closed self-recur suffix may write its exact parameter
        ;; home directly when the current owner dies at that producer. Counted
        ;; recurrence proof may admit a real direct call only when the closed
        ;; module proves its callee is a pure, nontrapping, call-free leaf.
        ;; This repository still does not execute compiled programs. A green
        ;; native suite here is encodings only, not that measurement.
        ;; 8a2bc4d sends straight-line call functions through the scanner:
        ;; call-crossing values live in preserved registers instead of stable
        ;; slots (+6.66% measured on the qualified call fixture); the
        ;; superseded allocate-call-live is deleted.
        ;; 4a75623 steers quotient-leaf values away from RAX/RDX, arming
        ;; the dead-quotient-save elision below it.
        ;; e266a86: the parallel copy's cycle-breaking temporary is carried
        ;; into the body only when something reserved it. Carried unreserved it
        ;; named the slot the body's first spill was then handed, and the next
        ;; cycle break stored over a live value -- measured on aiueos
        ;; hkdf-sha256.kotoba, whose `hmac-mode` passed the literal 92 as its
        ;; own context pointer (kotoba-mir ADR-0017).
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-mir
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotoba-mir.git"
         :git/sha "9d5b7950f0248eee948529217f7ead32aadb61a4"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-codegen
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotoba-codegen.git"
         :git/sha "3a7d7fc216408d7de53daaec6012aca1db4360b2"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-object
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotoba-object.git"
         :git/sha "9b53a444cfe5550af6b76eef494b4190b5e4e461"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/artifact
